Description: Validate proposed boot and encrypted swap layout before any disk jobs
Author: KythOS contributors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-16

Native guided, alongside, replacement and manual controls stay available. A
plain root can contain boot files. The signed GRUB path needs public /boot for
encrypted root. Selected swap must be encrypted when root is encrypted. Show a
visible native-page explanation, disable Next only for these invalid plans,
and defensively replace the partition queue with a failure job before writes.
No passphrases are copied or logged by this patch.

